{
	"VersionNumber": 1,
	"ResourceName": "okta_ip_allowlist",
	"Description": "Tuning control for $OKTA_TUNING: suppress Okta detections coming from source addresses you have vouched for. A row that is enabled and unexpired drops the event outright.\n\nFields: key,enabled,until_ymd,reason\n  - key: the bare source IP address, matched against src (clientIp, else the first hop of request.ipChain)\n  - enabled: 1 to apply the row, 0 to park it without deleting it\n  - until_ymd: YYYYMMDD expiry, compared against the event's published date; leave empty for a permanent exception\n  - reason: free text, so the next analyst knows why the exception exists\n\nCurrent contents:\nkey,enabled,until_ymd,reason\n203.0.113.10,1,,corporate NAT egress - permanently allowed\n198.51.100.20,1,20261231,vulnerability scanner - allowed until end of 2026\n\nUsage:\n$OKTA_RISK_SCORE\n$OKTA_TUNING",
	"Labels": [
